title: The Presidential Channel
subtitle: A signature, veto or photograph can change the opposition's leverage.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_presidential_channel_timer <= 0 and trz_blocked = 0 and president_name != "" and (presidential_channel_open = 1 or president_relation >= 25)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_presidential_channel_timer = 4
card-image: img/poland/deck_party.svg

= The Presidential Channel

[? if president_name = "Andrzej Duda": The Palace accepts a private briefing.
Duda's conflict with parts of PiS is real, but so is his dependence on its
electorate and institutions. A narrow opening can produce a signature, a
veto—or a photograph useful only to him. ?]

[? if president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski": Trzaskowski's Palace is an opposition institution
inside a PiS state. Access is easy; deciding whether Lewica is coordinating
with KO's President or surrendering its own programme is harder. ?]

[? if president_name != "Andrzej Duda" and president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski":
President **[+ president_name +]** has allowed a direct political channel.
Access does not guarantee a signature, and a Palace photograph can still cost
Lewica more than the meeting delivers. ?]

- @social_dossier
- @court_appeal
- @trz_veto_channel
- @trz_rights_channel
- @public_distance

@social_dossier
title: Offer a bill-by-bill social dossier
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Palace access grows; KO suspects an issue deal.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A serious legislative dossier requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; president_relation += 6; household_security += 3; government_delivery += 1; barons_dissent -= 1; ko_relation -= 3; public_trust += 1; pensioner_support += 3; public_sector_support += 1; news_headline = "The Palace accepts a Left social-policy dossier"

[? if president_name = "Andrzej Duda": Disability support, pensions, labour inspection and
public health are chosen because a presidential signature can be defended to
conservative voters. The channel is useful precisely because it is not an
alliance. ?]

[? if president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski": Disability support, labour inspection, public health and
local finance give the Palace a social agenda that is not only KO's
institutional conflict. The meeting is cooperation, not a coalition. ?]

[? if president_name != "Andrzej Duda" and president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski":
The dossier forces the current President to answer concrete proposals rather
than a party label. The channel remains transactional, not a coalition. ?]

- #poland_card_finish

@court_appeal
title: Ask the President to veto the next institutional escalation
subtitle: A lawful appeal tests his independence and risks a very public refusal.
view-if: president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: president_relation += 2; judicial_legitimacy += 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; pis_relation -= 3; progressive_credibility += 1; public_trust += 1; urban_progressive_support += 2; turnout_readiness += 1; news_headline = "The Left places the constitutional burden on the President"

The appeal distinguishes ordinary judgments from unlawfully captured bodies and
offers the President a narrow way back from escalation. If he refuses, the
refusal will belong to him.

- #poland_card_finish

@trz_veto_channel
title: Put the next PiS institutional statute on the veto list
subtitle: Stronger cohabitation front; every veto feeds the right's obstruction campaign.
view-if: president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: trz_vetoes += 1; president_relation += 5; judicial_legitimacy += 5; constitutional_restraint += 4; ko_relation += 2; pis_relation -= 4; trz_cohabitation_temperature += 4; trz_right_backlash += 3; pis_poll_momentum += 0.1; news_headline = "Lewica and the Palace add another statute to the veto list"

The legal brief separates repairable provisions from a package designed to
capture appointments. Trzaskowski promises the veto; PiS calls the meeting an
opposition government operating from the Palace.

- #poland_card_finish

@trz_rights_channel
title: Ask for written no-veto pledges on equality laws
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Abortion restoration and marriage equality get signatures in advance.
view-if: president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski"
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A common legislative package requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; trz_abortion_signature = 1; trz_marriage_signature = 1; trz_abortion_veto_policy = "Will sign abortion restoration"; trz_marriage_veto_policy = "Will sign marriage equality"; president_relation += 7; progressive_credibility += 5; feminist_trust += 4; psl_relation -= 3; trz_right_fragmentation += 3; trz_right_backlash += 6; far_right_agenda += 3; konf_poll_momentum += 0.25; news_headline = "The Palace issues written no-veto pledges on equality"

The pledges do not create 231 votes. They do remove the Presidency as an excuse
for deputies who claim a rights bill would be futile.

- #poland_card_finish

@public_distance
title: Refuse the Palace photograph
subtitle: Preserve opposition clarity and surrender a possible institutional lever.
on-arrival: president_relation -= 5; ko_relation += 2; progressive_credibility += 2; progressives_dissent -= 1; barons_dissent += 2; constitutional_restraint -= 1; public_trust += 1; young_support += 1; news_headline = "The Left declines a presidential display of independence"

[? if president_name = "Andrzej Duda": You will not help Duda perform autonomy while he
signs the rest of PiS's agenda. The democratic opposition applauds. A Palace
aide quietly closes the next available appointment. ?]

[? if president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski": Lewica refuses to become the junior press office of a KO
presidency. The party preserves its line and loses a direct veto channel. ?]

[? if president_name != "Andrzej Duda" and president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski":
Lewica refuses to turn Palace access into an endorsement of **[+
president_name +]**. The party preserves its line and loses a direct channel.
?]

- #poland_card_finish
